      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It would be nice if the .vrca files were encrypted or at least obfuscated in such a way that it would be extremely difficult to successfully crack the files off VRC's servers. For direct asset theft and the like, that's on the users to file a DMCA complaint. They are US based so they have to follow the us DMCA. If you take this route, VRChat has a legal obligation to investigate or they could be sued for infringement from the asset owner. Just be aware that you have to be the owner or legally allowed to act on behalf of the owner before filing such a complaint.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
